# Interaction System

> **Do NOT invent — fill this by reading the real codebase and interviewing the team.**
> This document defines ONE pattern per category, used everywhere.
> Consistency is non-negotiable: if a pattern is defined here, every surface uses it.
> If the codebase contradicts this document, the codebase is wrong — or this document needs updating.

---

## Form validation

> Define ONE rule for each question. Capture what the project actually does today (or decides to do).

**When does validation trigger?**
<< On blur? On submit? On change after first submit attempt? Describe the exact rule. >>

**How is an error displayed?**
<< Inline below the field? In a summary at the top? Both? What element, what position? >>

**Error message structure:**
<< What must every error message contain? (field name? cause? remedy?) Give a template. >>

**What happens to the submit button while the form has errors?**
<< Disabled? Enabled but shows errors on click? Something else? >>

**How are server-side errors (post-submit) shown?**
<< Same inline pattern? Separate banner? How are they cleared? >>

---

## Loading and async

**Page-level loading state:**
<< What does the user see while a full page is loading? Skeleton? Spinner? Nothing? >>

**Component-level loading state:**
<< What does a button look like when its action is in flight? Disabled + spinner? Text change? >>

**Optimistic updates:**
<< Does this product use them? If yes, what is the rollback behaviour on failure? >>

**Polling / streaming:**
<< Any surfaces that update in real time? How is "updating" communicated to the user? >>

